  "grammarTip": "The locative case answers 'where?' and always follows 'u' or 'na'. Masculine and neuter nouns typically add -u: autobus → u autobusu (on the bus), voz → u vozu (on the train), aerodrom → na aerodromu (at the airport). Some nouns pair with 'na' by convention even though they aren't open surfaces — na stanici (at the station) — while enclosed vehicles usually take 'u': u autobusu, u tramvaju, u taksiju.",
